[E0411] Error: a `for` walks a place, not a reference to it
    ╭─[ err/567_a_for_over_a_borrow/main.wip:11:14 ]
    │
 11 │     for ball in &var balls {
    │                 ─────┬────
    │                      ╰────── `&var` before what is walked
    │
    │ Help: remove the `&var`
    │
    │ Note: a `for` lends each element of what it walks: for writing where the place can be written, a `var` or a `&var` parameter, and for reading where not
────╯
